{
  "schema": "orca.head_envelope.v1",
  "id": "snapmaker-u1",
  "name": "Snapmaker U1 (stock quick-swap hotend, estimated)",
  "provenance": "Photo- and wiki-derived conservative estimate; calibrated=false. Structure from the U1 toolhead disassembly guide (https://wiki.snapmaker.com/en/snapmaker_u1/troubleshooting/toolhead_disassembly_and_reassembly: cover, male mount, extruder unit, hotend, control board) and the hot end replacement guide (https://wiki.snapmaker.com/en/snapmaker_u1/troubleshooting/hot_end_replacement_guide): integrated ceramic-heater hotend with silicone sock and finned heatsink, quick-swap 0.2-0.8 nozzles; teardown cover photo (https://support.snapmaker.com/hc/en-us/articles/36143490863383) shows the finned heatsink, sock, front-fan cover and rear extruder unit. The hotend column below z=40 reuses the measured Bambu P1S bands because the U1 hotend is the same integrated ceramic-heater class; the silicone sock and heater clip are widened by 1 mm to absorb the unknown U1 dimensions and the nozzle land/cone bands are the standard 0.4 mm geometry. Duct walls, fan shroud, cover, male mount, extruder unit and X gantry are generous photo-derived bands, not measurements; gantry underside estimated at z=34 to match the P1S envelope (uncertain). Margins 0.5 mm. Run the built-in clearance calibration and mark the copy calibrated before aggressive tilts. Nozzle-tip frame +X right, +Y rear, +Z up, mm. Selected 2026-11-13, checked 2026-11-13.",
